  "why": "Baselines come from pdftotext dumps of published PDFs, where paragraph boundaries are unreliable (two-column extraction merges and splits them). Sentence-scoped metrics are unaffected and are directly comparable to a .docx manuscript. Paragraph-scoped metrics -- FLOW and its no_connectives component -- are measured against a systematically deflated baseline, so a draft can exceed the FLOW p90 without being unusual. Report FLOW findings individually on their merits; do not gate on the rate.",
  "strata_agreement": "published (2023-26, n=116) and pre_llm (<2022-11, n=30) agree closely on every dimension, which is evidence these lexicons measure academic prose register rather than machine authorship. The two real gaps run the counter-intuitive way: recent papers use *less* filler (0.47 vs 0.94 /1k) and fewer unanchored pronouns (0.69 vs 1.01), consistent with heavier copy-editing rather than with generated text."
 }
